  "query_preview": "..\nIssued 259 PM CDT Wed Aug 12 2026\n\nFriday through Wednesday:\n\nRain and storms continue to lift northward through Friday\nmorning. As the warm front over the region begins to move away \nFriday afternoon and a surface high pressure system with upper-\nlevel ridging settling in, there is a potential for a break in \nPoPs. However, lingering high humidity Friday night could \nsustain the precipitation chances overnight (30-40%).\n\nFollowing this shift, a surface low from the Plains into the Great\nLakes region brings the chance of precipitation back Saturday\n(40-60%). The presence of a warm front and WAA favor these odds, \nbut there is uncertainty in severe potential. Instability behind \nthe warm front could create thunderstorm development, but low bulk\nshear and the jet stream remaining to the north does not favor a \nsevere pattern. Despite this chance at this point remaining\nunlikely, the location of the low and CAPE could cause severity.\n\nThe cold front following the warm late Saturday into Sunday could\nkeep the PoPs chances in the CWA, but upper-level zonal flow and a\nhigh pressure system moving in from the Plains will push a drier\nairmass into the region early next week.\n\nZawlocki",
